{"id":"h009","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? Insulin was first isolated at the University of Toronto.","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"Banting, Best, Macleod and Collip at the University of Toronto isolated insulin in 1921-1922.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.9,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The Toronto team showed insulin lowered blood sugar and kept diabetic animals and then humans alive.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.7,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The Toronto work is the standard account of insulin's discovery, and the 1923 Nobel Prize was awarded for it.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.8,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Nicolae Paulescu produced a pancreatic extract in Bucharest and published on its blood-sugar-lowering effect in 1921, before Toronto's published results.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-0.6,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Some historians question whether Toronto was truly first.","confidence":0.7,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.0996,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Paulescu's extract was less purified and not a reproducible, clinically usable preparation.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.6,"theta":1.2566,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The mainstream historical view credits Toronto with the isolation that made insulin usable as therapy, which is what most sources mean by the claim.","confidence":0.85,"lean":0.8,"theta":1.3352,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Paulescu's priority dispute is real but does not overturn the standard account.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.7,"theta":1.2566,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The claim is true in the conventional sense but not entirely uncontested.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.5,"theta":1.2566,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":-0.5,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J"